{"name":"Future Hair","hex":"#20b562","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"future","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The time ahead; those moments yet to be experienced.","Something that will happen in moments yet to come."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having to do with or occurring in the future."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/future"},{"term":"hair","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A pigmented filament of keratin which grows from a follicle on the skin of humans and other mammals.","The collection or mass of such growths growing from the skin of humans and animals, and forming a covering for any part or the whole body."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To remove the hair from.","To grow hair (where there was a bald spot)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hair"}],"entries":[{"title":"Future","blocks":[{"text":"The future is the time after the past and the present. Its arrival is considered inevitable due to the existence of time and the laws of physics. Due to the apparent nature of the reality and the unavoidability of the future, everything that currently exists and will exist can be categorized as either permanent, meaning that it will exist forever, or temporary, meaning that it will end. In the Occidental view, which uses a linear conception of time, the future is the portion of the projected timeline that is anticipated to occur. In special relativity, the future is considered absolute future, or the future light cone."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Zeitpyramide_2023_B.jpg/330px-Zeitpyramide_2023_B.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Future","wikidata":"Q344"},{"title":"Hair","blocks":[{"text":"Hair is a protein filament that grows from follicles found in the dermis. Hair is one of the distinguishing characteristics of mammals.\nThe human body, apart from areas of glabrous skin, is covered in follicles which produce thick terminal and fine vellus hair. Most common interest in hair is focused on hair growth, hair types, and hair care, but hair is also an important biomaterial primarily composed of protein, notably alpha-keratin."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Gray945.png/330px-Gray945.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hair","wikidata":"Q28472"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/MontreGousset001.jpg/500px-MontreGousset001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/MontreGousset001.jpg/500px-MontreGousset001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMontreGousset001.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Stanford_Torus_interior.jpg/500px-Stanford_Torus_interior.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Stanford_Torus_interior.jpg/1280px-Stanford_Torus_interior.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Stanford_Torus_interior.jpg/500px-Stanford_Torus_interior.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Project of an orbital colony Stanford torus, painted by Donald E. Davis","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStanford_Torus_interior.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Sortie_de_l%27op%C3%A9ra_en_l%27an_2000-2.jpg/500px-Sortie_de_l%27op%C3%A9ra_en_l%27an_2000-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/comm